# Fajr Quant - Project Rules

## Project overview
Fajr Quant is a stock analysis platform for the Indonesian stock market (IDX).
- Backend: Python 3.11 + FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + Celery
- Frontend: Next.js (TypeScript) + Tailwind + Recharts
- Database: MySQL / MariaDB
- Data sources: Stockbit (Exodus) API (token-based) + yfinance (fallback)

## Architecture rules
- All Stockbit HTTP calls MUST go through `backend/app/clients/stockbit.py` (or `base.py`).
  Never call the Exodus endpoints directly from services or routes.
- Data persistence MUST use SQLAlchemy models in `backend/app/models/`.
- Sensitive values (Stockbit token) MUST be encrypted at rest via `app/utils/encryption.py`.
- Technical analysis modules live in `app/services/technical/` and are registered in its `REGISTRY`.
- Bandarmology modules live in `app/services/bandarmology/` and are registered in its `REGISTRY`.
- Scoring logic lives in `app/services/scoring/`. Weights and thresholds MUST be configurable, not hardcoded in routes.
- Long-running work (data fetch, scoring, telegram digest) MUST run as Celery tasks in `app/workers/tasks.py`.

## Documentation rule (IMPORTANT)
Any change that affects: data flow, DB schema, Stockbit/yfinance endpoints, scoring
weights/formulas, AI prompt, or Telegram behavior MUST be accompanied by an update
to the relevant file in `docs/` AND an entry in `docs/CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.

## Style
- Python: type hints where practical, functions documented with short docstrings.
- No emojis in code or commit messages.
- Keep API responses JSON-serializable (use pydantic schemas in `app/api/schemas.py`).
- Frontend API base is `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (default `http://localhost:8000/api/v1`).
